# Wallet Sweeper - Environment Configuration

## Frontend Environment Variables

### Development (.env.development)
```bash
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
VITE_DEFAULT_DESTINATION_WALLET=0xYourTestAddress
VITE_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID=your_walletconnect_project_id
```

### Production (.env.production)
```bash
# Railway automatically sets PORT and NODE_ENV
VITE_API_URL=/api
VITE_DEFAULT_DESTINATION_WALLET=0xYourProductionAddress
VITE_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID=your_walletconnect_project_id
```

## Backend Environment Variables

### Development (.env.development.server)
```bash
# Server
PORT=3001
NODE_ENV=development
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# WalletSweeper Contracts (after deployment)
VITE_WALLET_SWEEPER_1=0xContractAddressEthereum
VITE_WALLET_SWEEPER_137=0xContractAddressPolygon
VITE_WALLET_SWEEPER_42161=0xContractAddressArbitrum
# ... add other chains as needed

# Optional: RPC URLs
ETH_RPC_URL=https://eth-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/YOUR_API_KEY
POLYGON_RPC_URL=https://polygon-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/YOUR_API_KEY
INFURA_API_KEY=your_infura_key

# Gas Buffer (default: 0.1 ETH in wei)
MIN_GAS_BUFFER=100000000000000000

# Default destination for sweeps
DEFAULT_DESTINATION_WALLET=0xYourSweepDestination
```

### Production (.env.production.server)
```bash
# Railway automatically sets these:
# - PORT (default 3001)
# - NODE_ENV=production

# Security
CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-domain.com

# WalletSweeper Contracts
VITE_WALLET_SWEEPER_1=0xContractAddressEthereum
VITE_WALLET_SWEEPER_137=0xContractAddressPolygon
VITE_WALLET_SWEEPER_42161=0xContractAddressArbitrum
# ... add other chains

# Optional but recommended
MIN_GAS_BUFFER=100000000000000000
DEFAULT_DESTINATION_WALLET=0xYourSweepDestination
```

## Railway Deployment Variables

Set these in Railway dashboard under "Variables":

```
NODE_ENV=production
VITE_DEFAULT_DESTINATION_WALLET=0xYourAddress
VITE_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID=your_id
VITE_WALLET_SWEEPER_1=0xYourContractAddress
CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-railway-domain.up.railway.app
VITE_WALLET_SWEEPER_137=0xYourPolygonContract
# ... etc
```

## Important Notes

1. **Frontend API URL**: 
   - Development: `http://localhost:3001`
   - Production: `/api` (Railway handles the proxy)

2. **CORS_ORIGIN**: 
   - Set to your domain in production
   - Allows only that domain to access the API

3. **Contract Addresses**: 
   - Format: `VITE_WALLET_SWEEPER_{CHAIN_ID}=0x...`
   - Deploy contracts first, then add addresses here

4. **Never commit `.env` files** - only use `.env.example`

5. **Railway automatically injects**: `PORT`, `NODE_ENV`

## Example Railway Setup

### Build Command
```bash
npm install && npm run build:all
```

### Start Command
```bash
npm run server:prod
```

### Environment Variables
```
NODE_ENV=production
VITE_DEFAULT_DESTINATION_WALLET=0x123abc...
VITE_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID=abc123...
CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-app.up.railway.app
```

Then Railway will:
1. Install dependencies
2. Build frontend and backend
3. Start server on auto-assigned PORT
4. Serve `/api` routes from backend
5. Serve `/` routes from frontend static files
